Package: kyberfrog
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Tristan Perrault <tritriper35@gmail.com>
Section: video
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://gitlab.com/kyber-frog/kyberfrog
Depends: libc6, libdrm2, libxcb1, libxcb-shm0, libwayland-client0, libpulse0
Description: Self-hosted low-latency LAN video transport (NDI alternative)
 KyberFrog creates transmitters and viewers from a web UI on :7700 to send
 video sources between machines over QUIC, a drop-in NDI replacement for the
 LAN. One app per machine; whether a box emits, receives, or both is set by the
 config and the web UI — there is no separate server and client build.
 .
 This package bundles the Kyber fork binaries (kycontroller / kyavserver /
 kyclient) and their shared libraries. On Linux a transmitter captures the
 screen via xcb / drm / wlroots / nvfbc; a viewer displays a remote stream.
